  "description": "HiQPdf Next Excel to PDF Converter for .NET (Multi-platform) is a component of the HiQPdf Next Library for .NET that enables accurate conversion of complex Excel documents to PDF and to Markdown.\n\nThe converter targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows, Linux and macOS, including Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Docker and Kubernetes.\n\nThis multi-platform metapackage installs the Windows x64 and Linux x64 runtimes.\n\nFor Windows ARM64, Linux ARM64 and macOS ARM64, the additional packages HiQPdf.Next.ExcelToPdf.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Next.ExcelToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.Next.ExcelToPdf.MacOS can be referenced on their own or alongside this package.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Windows 10, 11 and Windows Server 2016 to 2025 (x64)\n* Linux (x64) - Debian 11+, Ubuntu 20.04+ or equivalent\n* Windows, Linux and macOS (ARM64) - via additional packages\n* .NET 11.0, 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* .NET Framework 4.6.2 to 4.8.1\n* Azure, AWS and Google Cloud\n* Virtual Machines\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert Excel XLSX documents to PDF and to Markdown\n* Print layout, print area, page breaks and repeated rows from Excel\n* Page settings, headers and footers from Excel or custom settings\n* Charts, pictures and shapes from the workbook\n* Recalculate formulas and open password protected workbooks\n* Convert all worksheets or only the first, with or without titles\n* Keep the column widths and row heights from Excel\n* Generate PDF/A and PDF/UA documents\n* Add HTML headers, footers or stamps to the generated PDF\n* Encrypt, sign and set PDF viewer preferences for the generated PDF\n* Asynchronous methods for async and await\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.hiqpdf.com/hiqpdf-next-excel-xlsx-to-pdf-dotnet",
